================================================================================
Provenance
================================================================================

The kernel sources in `kernel/` are derived work. The chain is:

1. FlyDSL (https://github.com/ROCm/FlyDSL), Apache-2.0
   Copyright (c) 2026 FlyDSL Project Contributors

     kernels/gemm/gemm_bf16_gfx1250.py     dense gfx1250 TDM + WMMA NT GEMM
     kernels/gemm/gemm_common_gfx1250.py   LDS copy ops / pipeline fences

   These supplied the dense gfx1250 tile body that everything here is built on.

2. Primus-Turbo (https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Primus-Turbo)
   Copyright (c) 2026, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.

     primus_turbo/flydsl/grouped_gemm/grouped_gemm_bf16_kernel.py  (gfx950 / MI355X)

   This supplied the grouped control logic: the M-tile table, per-expert
   rebasing, the tile -> (expert, block_m, block_n) decode, and the XCD remap.

   Note that Primus-Turbo as a whole is MIT-licensed, but its FlyDSL grouped-GEMM
   kernels carry an Apache-2.0 header because of the FlyDSL provenance above.
   The Apache-2.0 header is the one that governs the files in `kernel/`, and it
   has been preserved verbatim at the top of each file.

3. This repository
   Copyright (c) 2026, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.

   The gfx1250 / MI455X port itself (WMMA, wave32, TDM, the native NN pipeline
   built on `ds_load_tr16_b128`), plus the measurement harnesses, probes and
   documentation.

================================================================================
Licensing of the documentation
================================================================================

`docs/`, `README.md` and the raw data under `results/` are covered by the same
Apache-2.0 license as the code, rather than by a separate documentation license.

Reasoning: the documentation is not independent prose, it is a description of
the code and of measurements taken from it, and a downstream consumer who
vendors `kernel/` will usually want the pitfalls and the tuning rationale to
travel with it. A second license on the prose would force them to track two
sets of terms for one artifact. Apache-2.0 covers documentation ("the Work"
includes documentation in Section 1) and its attribution requirements are
satisfied by keeping this NOTICE file.

================================================================================
Third-party documents referenced but NOT redistributed
================================================================================

The ISA investigation in `docs/03-isa-investigation.md` cites the

    "AMD Instinct CDNA5 Instruction Set Architecture Reference Guide"

published by AMD at

    https://www.amd.com/content/dam/amd/en/documents/instinct-tech-docs/
    instruction-set-architectures/amd-instinct-cdna5-instruction-set-architecture.pdf

That document is **not** included in this repository. Section references are
given by section number and heading so they can be followed in the published
PDF. `probes/isa/pdf_extract.py` reproduces the text extraction that the
original investigation used, if you want the line-addressable form.
